  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Sophorabioside may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular pathways. The compound is identified as a target of DNA polymerase iota, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Scortechinone A and Macaflavone II. These latter two compounds are also linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential pathway where Sophorabioside may influence the activity of DNA polymerase iota, which is subsequently targeted by other molecules that engage with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The scores for the relationships suggest a moderate level of confidence in this connection, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights a possible regulatory or inhibitory role of Sophorabioside in the pathway leading to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the nature of this interaction.",
